    "attack_surfaces": [
      {
        "function": "eat_cookie",
        "input": "random index from /dev/urandom",
        "operation": "FREE + pointer swap-remove without NULL",
        "risk": "HIGH",
        "reason": "free(msg[idx]) is called, then msg[idx]=msg[cookie_num-1] (copy happens BEFORE cookie_num--). Freed pointer is NOT set to NULL. When idx==cookie_num-1, self-assign leaves freed pointer in slot that becomes out-of-range. When idx<cookie_num-1, freed pointer overwritten by last element, but last slot still holds same pointer (now out of range). S2 should analyze whether a sequence of operations can leave a freed pointer accessible within valid index range."
